        </li>
        <li>The App is free and provided "as is".</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Not an Emergency Service</h2>
    <p>
        The App doesn't contact the police, emergency services, or anyone other
        than the recipients you set up. Don't rely on it in place of calling for
        help. Notifications are ordinary emails, and your recipients may not see
        them in time, or at all.
    </p>

    <h2>No Guarantee of Upload or Delivery</h2>
    <p>
        The App records in short clips and tries to upload each one to your Google
        Drive soon after it finishes. Clips may upload late, or not at all, and
        emails may be delayed or not sent. This can happen for reasons including:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>No or poor network connection, or a connection that drops</li>
        <li>
            Your phone being turned off, damaged, out of battery, or taken before
            a clip finishes or uploads
        </li>
        <li>
            iOS limiting or stopping work the App does in the background, or
            taking the camera away when the App leaves the screen
        </li>
        <li>Your Google Drive running out of storage</li>
        <li>
            Google limiting, refusing, or failing requests, or your Google account
            being signed out, restricted, or suspended
        </li>
        <li>
            Your account or organization not allowing link sharing, so recipients
            can't open your recordings
        </li>
        <li>Recipients' email providers filtering or delaying emails</li>
        <li>Bugs in the App</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The part of a recording still being captured when something goes wrong
        may be lost. Check that the App works the way you expect before you need
        it, for example by sending a test email from Settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Recording laws.</strong> Many places restrict recording
            people, and some require everyone's consent before recording audio.
            You're responsible for knowing and following the laws that apply
            where you record, and for how you use your recordings.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Recipients.</strong> Only add people who are happy to receive
            emails from you. Emails are sent from your own Gmail account, so
            Google's rules for your account apply to them.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Shared links.</strong> When the App emails people about a
            recording, it makes that recording's Drive folder viewable by anyone
            with the link, as described in our{" "}
            <a href="/just-capture/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>. You're
            responsible for who you send it to. We can't control what others do
            with a link or a recording once they have it.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Lawful use.</strong> Don't use the App to harass, stalk, or
            invade the privacy of others, or for anything illegal.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Your Google account.</strong> Keep your phone and Google
            account secure. Anyone who can use them may be able to see your
            recordings and settings.
        </li>
    </ul>

